---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---
<section class="section" id="features">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <p class="label">What's inside</p>
        <h2 class="h2">Built for the docs you actually ship.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="lead">From a private runbook to a public API reference: the same check, with the rules each one needs.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bento">
      <article class="tile span-4" data-reveal>
        <span class="kicker">publico · publicado</span>
        <h3>Publish docs without leaking your code</h3>
        <p>Public pages can't carry internal paths or copied source, and they still need checking. Store the link outside the text: readers see clean prose, CI verifies both the sentence and the code.</p>
        <figure style="margin-top:20px"><div class="scroll"><img src={`${base}assets/published-docs.svg`} alt="Diagram: the public page shows only prose; the link from guide.md line 12 to validate_payment lives in the seal file; check verifies the sentence and the private code" width="960" height="300" loading="lazy"></div></figure>
        <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/publicado.py#IndiceCopias dockeeper/motor.py#vincular -->
      </article>

      <article class="tile span-2" data-reveal style="--d:80ms">
        <span class="kicker">syntax</span>
        <h3>Anchor it your way</h3>
        <ul class="syntax">
          <li><code>&#91;&#91;pay.ts#validate&#93;&#93;</code><span>symbol</span></li>
          <li><code>&#91;&#91;pay.ts:147&#93;&#93;</code><span>line</span></li>
          <li><code>&lt;!-- dockeeper: … --&gt;</code><span>hidden</span></li>
          <li><code>dockeeper link</code><span>outside</span></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="tile span-2" data-reveal>
        <span class="kicker">--solo · --sin</span>
        <h3>Check one part at a time</h3>
        <p>Point <code>--solo</code> at code and every doc that talks about it is checked. Point it at a doc and it keeps the code it cites.</p>
        <pre class="code">dockeeper check --solo src/payments</pre>
        <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/alcance.py#Alcance -->
      </article>

      <article class="tile span-2" data-reveal style="--d:80ms">
        <span class="kicker">why</span>
        <h3>The why, never invented</h3>
        <p>Decisions come from your git history. If the reason isn't there, the docs say so.</p>
<pre class="code"><span class="k">Decision:</span> seal lives in its own file
<span class="k">Why:</span> public pages must not leak paths</pre>
        <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/porque.py#historial -->
      </article>

      <article class="tile span-2" data-reveal style="--d:160ms">
        <span class="kicker">the skill</span>
        <h3>Your agent's loop</h3>
        <p>One rule, every verifiable claim gets an anchor, and one workflow it can't skip.</p>
        <div class="loop"><span>audit</span><i>→</i><span>write</span><i>→</i><span>scan</span><i>→</i><span>check</span><i>→</i><span>fix</span></div>
        <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/motor.py#comprobar -->
      </article>

      <article class="tile span-3" id="review" data-reveal>
        <span class="kicker">review · post-commit</span>
        <h3>Docs that keep up with every commit</h3>
        <p>After each commit, <code>review</code> lists the claims it touched, the new code nothing documents yet and the decisions nobody wrote down. As a git hook it never blocks: your agent reads it and updates the docs as it goes.</p>
<pre class="code"><span class="c">$ git commit -m "feat: refunds"</span>
dockeeper review · changes since HEAD~1
<span class="v-CHANGED">CHANGED</span>  docs/payments.md:3 → validate_payment
<span class="s">new</span>      src/payments.py#refund (3 lines)
Decisions not documented yet:
  refunds reuse the payment validation</pre>
        <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/revision.py#revisar -->
      </article>

      <article class="tile span-3" id="monorepos" data-reveal style="--d:80ms">
        <span class="kicker">audit · monorepos</span>
        <h3>Whole repositories, monorepos included</h3>
        <p><code>audit</code> finds every package by its manifest, from <code>package.json</code> to <code>go.mod</code> or <code>Cargo.toml</code>. The agent writes the root map first, then documents one package at a time, so even a huge repository fits.</p>
<pre class="code"><span class="c">$ dockeeper audit</span>
Packages (4): document one at a time
apps/web/          1/2  README.md
packages/api/      0/3  no README  <span class="v-CHANGED">← undocumented</span>
services/billing/  0/2  no README  <span class="v-CHANGED">← undocumented</span>
libs/core/         0/1  no README  <span class="v-CHANGED">← undocumented</span></pre>
        <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/paquetes.py#detectar -->
      </article>

      <article class="tile span-6" id="ci" data-reveal>
        <span class="kicker">continuous integration</span>
        <h3>Keep it true on every pull request</h3>
        <p>The repository is also a GitHub Action. Anywhere else, it's two lines of shell. No green when nothing was checked.</p>
        <div class="ci-grid">
<pre class="code"><span class="c"># .github/workflows/docs.yml</span>
<span class="k">jobs:</span>
  <span class="k">dockeeper:</span>
    <span class="k">runs-on:</span> ubuntu-latest
    <span class="k">steps:</span>
      - <span class="k">uses:</span> <span class="s">actions/checkout@v6</span>
      - <span class="k">uses:</span> <span class="s">Nokky21/DocKeeper@v0.1.0</span></pre>
<pre class="code"><span class="c"># any other CI</span>
git clone --depth 1 \
  https://github.com/Nokky21/DocKeeper.git /tmp/dk
python3 /tmp/dk/bin/dockeeper check</pre>
        </div>
        <!-- dockeeper: dockeeper/motor.py#FALLOS -->
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
